09:28.567 --> 09:30.227
Let's see... Miyamizu-san?

09:31.157 --> 09:31.557
Yes.

09:32.887 --> 09:35.697
Oh, so you remember your name today.

09:38.647 --> 09:40.017
You don't remember?

09:41.027 --> 09:41.697
No.

09:42.177 --> 09:46.227
Yesterday you forgot where your desk
and locker were.

09:46.527 --> 09:49.397
You had bedhead and no ribbon.

09:52.167 --> 09:54.367
What? No way. Really?

09:54.647 --> 09:56.687
It was like you had amnesia.

09:57.077 --> 10:01.637
Well, I do feel like
I've been in a strange dream lately...

10:01.927 --> 10:04.407
A dream about someone else's life?

10:05.937 --> 10:07.697
I can't remember clearly.

10:08.307 --> 10:10.117
I know! That was...

10:10.727 --> 10:11.957
your previous life!

10:12.117 --> 10:16.207
Or maybe your subconscious
linked to the Everett multiverse...

10:16.247 --> 10:17.537
Stay out of this.

10:17.567 --> 10:20.917
Oh! Tessie, did you write that
in my notebook?

10:22.897 --> 10:23.967
Nothing.

10:25.407 --> 10:28.677
But Mitsuha, you really were
a bit weird yesterday.

10:29.127 --> 10:30.767
You been feeling alright?

10:32.287 --> 10:33.397
That's so strange.

10:34.017 --> 10:35.377
I feel just fine.

10:35.477 --> 10:36.977
Maybe it's stress?

10:37.137 --> 10:39.567
The ritual is coming up, isn't it?

10:39.617 --> 10:41.797
Aw, don't remind me!

10:42.147 --> 10:44.567
I can't stand this town anymore.

10:45.127 --> 10:47.087
It's too small and close-knit.

10:47.397 --> 10:50.757
I just want to graduate and go to Tokyo.

10:50.817 --> 10:55.137
I don't blame you.
There's really nothing in this town.

10:57.247 --> 10:59.317
Trains come every two hours.

10:59.507 --> 11:01.327
Convenience store closes at 9PM.

11:01.537 --> 11:03.347
No bookstore. No dentist.

11:03.477 --> 11:05.977
M{*\fax-0.145}o{*\fax-0.14}m{*\fax-0.135}m{*\fax-0.13}a{*\fax-0.125}'{*\fax-0.12}s {*\fax-0.11}P{*\fax-0.105}ub

11:03.477 --> 11:05.977
The Last Tap{Broken Hearts Club}{Some other name that explains that this pub is a place to go to get over past flings}

11:03.557 --> 11:05.857
But two pubs for some reason.

11:06.037 --> 11:07.187
Can't get a job.

11:07.217 --> 11:08.337
Can't get married.

11:08.407 --> 11:10.277
Can't even see the sun when it gets late.

11:12.527 --> 11:13.767
Give me a break!

11:13.797 --> 11:14.467
What?

11:15.987 --> 11:18.357
I mean... How about we stop by a café?

11:18.357 --> 11:19.747
What? A café?

11:18.837 --> 11:19.647
Really?

11:20.127 --> 11:21.207
Where!?

11:25.377 --> 11:26.547
Hello.

11:26.817 --> 11:27.887
Hello.

11:33.137 --> 11:34.497
This is a café?

11:34.767 --> 11:36.247
You knew there wasn't one.

11:36.997 --> 11:38.867
Mitsuha just went home.

11:40.577 --> 11:42.727
Things must be rough for her.

11:42.997 --> 11:45.107
Well, she's got a big role to play.

11:45.537 --> 11:46.327
Yeah.

11:49.747 --> 11:51.077
Hey, Tessie?

11:53.057 --> 11:55.237
What are you doing after you graduate?

11:55.927 --> 11:57.157
What's this?

11:57.527 --> 11:58.577
You asking about my future?

12:00.497 --> 12:01.267
Nothing special.

12:01.927 --> 12:05.297
Nothing special. I'll probably keep on
living a normal life in this town.

12:21.807 --> 12:23.667
I'd rather do that too.

12:24.127 --> 12:26.367
It's too soon for you yet, Yotsuha.

12:26.787 --> 12:28.517
Listen to the thread's voice.

12:29.267 --> 12:31.907
When you keep twining like that,

12:32.467 --> 12:36.197
emotions will start flowing between you and the thread.

12:36.887 --> 12:38.197
Threads don't talk.

12:38.367 --> 12:40.327
She means "Concentrate."

12:40.647 --> 12:42.687
1,000 years of Itomori's history

12:43.367 --> 12:46.147
is etched into our braided chords.

12:46.547 --> 12:47.247
Listen.

12:47.827 --> 12:50.387
200 years ago...

12:50.517 --> 12:51.747
Here she goes again.

12:52.177 --> 12:56.047
Sandal maker Mayugoro's bathroom

12:56.467 --> 12:58.597
caught on fire and burned down this whole area.

12:59.317 --> 13:01.637
The shrine and old documents were destroyed.

13:02.707 --> 13:04.177
And this is known as...

13:04.197 --> 13:05.567
The Great Fire of Mayugoro.

13:05.807 --> 13:06.257
Right.

13:06.927 --> 13:10.007
The fire has his name? Poor Mayugoro.

13:10.977 --> 13:14.367
So the meaning of our festivals became unknown,

13:14.497 --> 13:16.367
and only the form lived on.

13:17.857 --> 13:21.377
But even if words are lost, tradition should still be handed down.

13:21.717 --> 13:25.637
That's the important task we at Miyamizu Shrine have.

13:28.967 --> 13:32.437
But that foolish son-in-law...

13:33.967 --> 13:37.667
As if leaving Shinto priesthood and this house weren't enough,

13:38.337 --> 13:40.567
now politics? He's hopeless.

13:41.297 --> 13:43.297
Have another, my friend.

13:46.657 --> 13:49.087
I'm counting on your help again.

13:49.157 --> 13:50.447
Don't you worry.

13:50.627 --> 13:54.337
You'll have votes from the Kadoiri and Sakagami Districts.

13:54.277 --> 13:55.407
How's it going with her?

13:55.667 --> 13:56.897
It's not that easy.

13:59.297 --> 14:01.327
I smell corruption.

14:01.537 --> 14:02.817
Don't be ridiculous.

14:04.467 --> 14:05.957
Bring us a few more hot saké.

14:06.047 --> 14:06.807
Okay.

14:07.367 --> 14:09.797
Katsuhiko, work on the site this weekend.

14:10.017 --> 14:11.927
Learn how to use explosives.

14:12.167 --> 14:12.757
Yeah.

14:13.407 --> 14:14.357
Can't hear you!

14:14.517 --> 14:15.127
Yes!

14:28.967 --> 14:31.397
We both have it rough, don't we?

14:50.117 --> 14:52.897
Is that Yotsuha-chan? She's all grown up.

14:53.167 --> 14:55.587
They're both pretty like their mother.

14:57.537 --> 14:58.017
Hey.

14:58.897 --> 14:59.427
Hey.

15:32.197 --> 15:34.097
It's the oldest saké in the world.

15:35.297 --> 15:40.247
By chewing on rice, spitting it out, and letting it ferment, it becomes alcohol.

15:40.647 --> 15:41.987
"Kuchikamizake."

15:42.767 --> 15:45.797
Do the gods really appreciate saké made that way?

15:45.927 --> 15:46.997
Of course they do.

15:49.567 --> 15:51.607
Hey, look. It's Miyamizu.

15:57.607 --> 15:59.527
Ew! I could never do that!

15:59.927 --> 16:01.667
Isn't she embarrassed?

16:01.687 --> 16:02.897
I can't believe it.

16:17.617 --> 16:19.647
Cheer up, Onee-chan.

16:20.367 --> 16:22.887
Who cares if a few classmates saw you?

16:22.917 --> 16:25.637
Must be nice being a carefree little kid.

16:26.207 --> 16:30.977
Why not sell lots of kuchikamizake and use the money to go to Tokyo?

16:31.077 --> 16:33.397
Where do you get such ideas?

16:33.587 --> 16:36.247
Sell it with photos and behind-the-scenes videos.

16:36.467 --> 16:38.967
Name it "Shrine Maiden's Saké" or somethin’.

16:39.317 --> 16:40.247
You'll make money!

