01:30:20.687 --> 01:30:23.757
I swear I could smell the scent of yours

01:30:24.727 --> 01:30:27.517
And in the way that you walked

01:30:28.027 --> 01:30:31.437
I could hear that bright laughter of yours

01:30:32.007 --> 01:30:35.287
Since one day you will disappear

01:30:33.767 --> 01:30:37.887
I can't remember your name with this.

01:30:36.307 --> 01:30:39.257
I'll keep every part of you

01:30:40.087 --> 01:30:44.007
Make sure that it's burned into the back of my eyes

01:30:44.007 --> 01:30:46.797
It's not a right that I'm due

01:30:47.727 --> 01:30:52.507
My duty that is must have been kept

01:30:51.567 --> 01:30:52.327
Dad!

01:30:54.927 --> 01:30:55.477
Mitsuha?

01:30:55.567 --> 01:30:56.257
Onee-chan?

01:30:56.977 --> 01:30:58.497
Not you again...

01:31:02.767 --> 01:31:06.007
lt was almost as if it were
a scene from a dream.

01:31:06.567 --> 01:31:10.387
Nothing more, nothing less
than a beautiful view.

01:31:10.677 --> 01:31:14.757
Words like "tomorrow" or "future" or "fate"

01:31:14.757 --> 01:31:18.787
No matter how far they extend their hands

01:31:18.787 --> 01:31:22.617
We breathe, we dream, we raise our love

01:31:22.617 --> 01:31:26.497
In a timeless land that is far out of reach

01:31:26.497 --> 01:31:30.367
Even the second, hour hands of the clock

01:31:30.367 --> 01:31:34.317
They look at us sideways as they tick and tock

01:31:34.317 --> 01:31:37.827
How I hope to have forever to spend

01:31:37.827 --> 01:31:41.857
This life, no, all future lives

01:31:41.857 --> 01:31:48.507
Right here in this world with you

01:32:26.857 --> 01:32:28.857
{}

01:32:42.117 --> 01:32:47.967
What am I doing here?

01:33:20.477 --> 01:33:22.887
I'm always searching for something.

01:33:24.257 --> 01:33:27.747
This feeling has possessed me
for some time.

01:33:30.247 --> 01:33:32.207
I applied because...

01:33:32.227 --> 01:33:33.957
The landscapes people live in...

01:33:33.967 --> 01:33:35.567
To build a city's landscape...

01:33:35.847 --> 01:33:39.457
You never know when Tokyo
might disappear as well.

01:33:40.017 --> 01:33:45.667
So I want to help build landscapes that
leave heartwarming memories...

01:33:48.257 --> 01:33:50.277
How many interviews have you had?

01:33:50.507 --> 01:33:51.687
I haven't kept track.

01:33:51.717 --> 01:33:54.207
- Can't see you landing a job.
- Thanks a lot!

01:33:54.227 --> 01:33:55.727
Maybe it's because of that suit.

01:33:55.927 --> 01:33:57.317
We're not that different!

01:33:58.007 --> 01:33:59.857
- I have 2 job offers.
- I have 8.

01:34:03.537 --> 01:34:03.657
You have a new message

01:34:03.657 --> 01:34:03.787
You have a new message

01:34:03.787 --> 01:34:03.907
You have a new message

01:34:03.907 --> 01:34:04.037
You have a new message

01:34:04.037 --> 01:34:04.157
You have a new message

01:34:04.157 --> 01:34:04.287
You have a new message

01:34:04.287 --> 01:34:07.417
You have a new message

01:34:05.807 --> 01:34:10.467
I'm not sure if I'm
searching for a person or a place,

01:34:11.797 --> 01:34:16.597
or if I'm just searching for a job.

01:34:18.087 --> 01:34:20.337
Oh, you're job-hunting.

01:34:20.527 --> 01:34:22.007
I haven't had much luck.

01:34:23.457 --> 01:34:24.977
Maybe it's because of that suit.

01:34:25.667 --> 01:34:26.977
Does it look that bad?

01:34:32.047 --> 01:34:34.007
What brings you here today?

01:34:34.567 --> 01:34:39.267
I came nearby for work
so I figured I'd say hi to you.

01:34:39.447 --> 01:34:42.947
8 years since the comet disaster

01:34:42.017 --> 01:34:45.537
We went to Itomori once, didn't we?

01:34:46.127 --> 01:34:49.167
You were still in high school, so it was...

01:34:50.167 --> 01:34:51.157
- Five years ago.

01:34:51.217 --> 01:34:51.967
- That long?

01:34:53.007 --> 01:34:55.507
Seems like I've forgotten a lot.

01:34:57.137 --> 01:35:01.237
I, too, no longer remember much
from back then.

01:35:02.817 --> 01:35:07.267
Maybe we had a disagreement; the other two
returned to Tokyo without me.

01:35:08.177 --> 01:35:11.157
I spent the night alone
on some mountain.

01:35:11.827 --> 01:35:13.077
That's about all I remember.

01:35:16.067 --> 01:35:19.127
But at one point,
I was inexplicably drawn

01:35:19.637 --> 01:35:22.447
to the events surrounding that comet.

01:35:25.047 --> 01:35:27.967
Half of a comet destroyed a town
in that disaster.

01:35:28.997 --> 01:35:35.257
Evacuation of residents to high school grounds confirmed.

01:35:29.167 --> 01:35:32.917
But most of the town's residents 
were miraculousy unhurt.

01:35:34.087 --> 01:35:37.277
The entire town happened to be
holding an emergency drill

01:35:35.507 --> 01:35:37.107
0 Deaths 
104 Wounded

01:35:37.277 --> 01:35:39.247
An unprecedented natural disaster

01:35:38.277 --> 01:35:41.527
and most of its residents were outside
the blast zone.

01:35:40.257 --> 01:35:42.257
Residents safe

01:35:42.257 --> 01:35:43.637
Disaster foretold!?

01:35:42.917 --> 01:35:46.657
The sheer luck and coincidence
sparked various rumors.

01:35:43.637 --> 01:35:45.097
A Mystery for the Ages

01:35:46.517 --> 01:35:49.517
Mayor Miyamizu's Hidden Agenda

01:35:47.667 --> 01:35:51.927
I intently read those articles back then.

01:35:49.537 --> 01:35:51.537
Mysterious explosion 
at the substation

01:35:53.137 --> 01:35:58.767
What had caught my interest
so much is now a mystery to me.

01:36:00.677 --> 01:36:03.637
I didn't even know anybody in that town.

01:36:06.037 --> 01:36:08.447
Thanks for today. This is far enough.

01:36:10.147 --> 01:36:15.237
You be happy someday too.

01:36:19.167 --> 01:36:24.127
I feel like I'm always searching
for something, for someone.

01:36:33.077 --> 01:36:34.037
Construction company job interview

01:36:36.837 --> 01:36:39.987
I want to go to another bridal fair.

01:36:40.007 --> 01:36:41.587
They're all the same.

01:36:41.937 --> 01:36:43.477
Shinto-style is nice too.

01:36:43.777 --> 01:36:45.637
You wanted a wedding in a chapel.

01:36:46.867 --> 01:36:48.277
Oh, and Tessie.

01:36:48.947 --> 01:36:52.597
Lose the beard before the wedding.
I'll lose a few pounds for you, 'kay?

01:36:53.407 --> 01:36:55.137
You're saying that while eating a cake?

01:36:55.527 --> 01:36:57.087
I'll start tomorrow.

01:37:41.947 --> 01:37:42.507
Itomori, the Town that Vanished

01:37:43.947 --> 01:37:45.407
October 4, 2013 - Itomori vanished.

01:37:45.487 --> 01:37:47.367
Kadoiri Bridge

01:37:48.107 --> 01:37:48.867
Itomori Elementary School

01:37:50.577 --> 01:37:51.867
Miyamizu Shrine

01:37:56.167 --> 01:37:58.257
Why does the scenery

01:37:59.557 --> 01:38:03.447
of a town that no longer exists
wring my heart so?

